## Control {{controlId}}: Session Lock with Pattern-Hiding Displays

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization uses session lock with pattern-hiding displays to prevent access and viewing of data after a period of inactivity within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant. Session lock enforcement is implemented through Intune device configuration policies, Conditional Access session controls, and Windows Group Policy settings that activate screen locks with pattern-hiding after the organization-defined inactivity timeout.

{{#if deviceConfigurationsActive}}
Intune enforces session lock through {{deviceConfigurationsCount}} device configuration policies. Policies configure automatic screen lock activation after the defined inactivity period, requiring re-authentication to resume the session. Pattern-hiding is enforced through lock screen display settings that conceal previously visible information with a blank screen or organizational logo overlay. Windows devices apply local Group Policy settings for screen saver timeout and password-protected resume.
{{else}}
Intune device configuration policies for session lock have not been configured. Session lock relies on default Windows settings pending policy deployment.
{{/if}}

